.TH sextant-gui 1 "sextant-gui 1.1.5"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
sextant-gui \- desktop SSH dashboard & server manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sextant-gui
.RI [ command ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sextant-gui
is the desktop client of Sextant, built with Fyne. It shows the same
dashboard as the terminal client, with a real terminal per host (rendered from
the built-in VT emulator), an SFTP browser with an in-app file editor, live
metrics, snippets that run across hosts, port forwards and a one-click SSH key
setup wizard.
.PP
The terminal client is
.BR sextant (1).
Both read and write the same JSON configuration, so hosts created in one
appear in the other.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B sync
Push or pull the encrypted configuration bundle
.RB ( push | pull " with " --local " or " --webdav ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SEXTANT_PORTABLE
When set to
.BR 1 ,
configuration is stored next to the executable. A file named
.B sextant.portable
next to the executable has the same effect.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
On Linux, if the window does not appear under Wayland, start with
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY=
to fall back to X11.
.SH FILES
See
.BR sextant (1)
for the configuration files; both clients use the same directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sextant (1),
.BR ssh (1)
